bpf: x86-64 JIT for l4h

The l4h x86_64 guest builds arch/x86/net with arch/l4h/x86/bpf_jit.c,
which places the images within rel32 reach of the kernel and patches
code without int3.  What the JIT needs and l4h does not have:

- exception tables: a fault of the guest kernel stops the guest, so
  programs with BPF_PROBE_MEM loads are left to the interpreter (which
  checks the address first), and arena accesses are not offered;
- %gs-based per-CPU data: no per-CPU instructions or private stacks;
- bpf_timed_may_goto.S, whose headers assume x86 per-CPU assembly.

The address of a callback (BPF_PSEUDO_FUNC) is loaded with a movabs
whatever its value: the verifier's stand-in for it, MODULES_VADDR, is
above all of RAM, the images below the kernel, and an instruction that
shrank in the last pass failed the program ("bpf_jit: fatal error").

--- a/arch/x86/net/Makefile
+++ b/arch/x86/net/Makefile
@@ -6,5 +6,8 @@
